[Music]  if you're a data-driven enterprise  you've likely been met with an explosion  of data growth in recent years and need  to find the best way to store all your  terabytes and petabytes at scale Google  Cloud Storage allows worldwide storage  and retrieval of any amount of data at  any time you can use Google Cloud  Storage for a range of scenarios  including serving website content  storing data for archival and disaster  recovery or distributing large data  objects to users via direct download in  this hands-on lab cloud storage  QuickStart console you will learn how to  use the Google cloud platform console to  create a storage bucket then upload  objects create folders and subfolders  and make those objects publicly  accessible data doesn't just mean rows  and columns and numbers anymore you may  want to store unstructured data like  messages documents multimedia files  webpages and so on whatever your storage  requirements are security availability  and cost will be your three  considerations Cloud Storage aims to  meet all of these requirements next up  on our quest is cloud I am QuickStart  [Music]

